  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116360",
      "title": "Implementing App-wide Error Management",
      "lectureOrder": 236,
      "videoOrder": 225,
      "sourceHash": "9ac6088d00e61195eff6198200c4f8cb6ac93acde4f4bcc77197ae98a807cb18",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.466,
          "end": 2.166,
          "en": "So we improved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.166,
          "end": 5.3,
          "en": "the optimistic updating behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.3,
          "end": 8.633,
          "en": "Now if we had an error as we had before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.633,
          "end": 10.933,
          "en": "if I briefly bring back that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.933,
          "end": 16.133,
          "en": "and I restart that backend, if we had that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.133,
          "end": 21.033,
          "en": "then of course as you saw before, adding places would fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.033,
          "end": 25.566,
          "en": "And if I tried to add a place like the African savannah,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.566,
          "end": 29,
          "en": "it would show up here briefly, but then it would be removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 32.066,
          "en": "Now of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.066,
          "end": 36.366,
          "en": "that's a better experience than having this incorrect UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.366,
          "end": 37.7,
          "en": "which we had before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.7,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "but it's not the best possible experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.066,
          "end": 43.566,
          "en": "Instead, it would be nice to also show the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.566,
          "end": 47.466,
          "en": "some error message if something goes wrong here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.466,
          "end": 50.166,
          "en": "But at the moment I do indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.1,
          "end": 54.233,
          "en": "throw an error observable that contains an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.233,
          "end": 55.933,
          "en": "with an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.933,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "But it's important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 61,
          "en": "that addPlaceToUserPlaces is called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "from inside the available places Component, here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 70,
          "en": "And I don't actually want to show the error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70,
          "end": 72.166,
          "en": "We could do that, but I don't wanna do it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.166,
          "end": 74.033,
          "en": "in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.033,
          "end": 77.333,
          "en": "That's why I'm currently not handling that error case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.333,
          "end": 79.166,
          "en": "even though we could.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.166,
          "end": 80.166,
          "en": "And therefore at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.166,
          "end": 82.633,
          "en": "we're not seeing any error message anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.633,
          "end": 86.633,
          "en": "Now again, as always, there are different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.633,
          "end": 91.533,
          "en": "of improving this situation and of handling this situation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.533,
          "end": 94.13300000000001,
          "en": "But here I'll go for an approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.13300000000001,
          "end": 96.733,
          "en": "where I'll use an extra Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.733,
          "end": 100.033,
          "en": "and service for managing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.033,
          "end": 103.366,
          "en": "And that's why attached you find a shared zip file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.366,
          "end": 106.333,
          "en": "which you should download and extract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.333,
          "end": 108.666,
          "en": "And then you should add this shared folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.666,
          "end": 111.96600000000001,
          "en": "into your app folder next to places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.9,
          "end": 116.333,
          "en": "And this shared folder then contains a modal Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.233,
          "end": 120.566,
          "en": "and an error-modal Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.566,
          "end": 123.766,
          "en": "which uses the modal Component in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.766,
          "end": 127.766,
          "en": "And both Components then use some features you saw before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.766,
          "end": 131.133,
          "en": "in this course already for receiving a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.133,
          "end": 134.766,
          "en": "and message that can be output here in the error-modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.766,
          "end": 138.833,
          "en": "and for selecting the dialogue element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.833,
          "end": 141.333,
          "en": "that can be found here in the modal Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.433,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "to show this modal dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "By the way, the dialogue element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 151.36599999999999,
          "en": "is a standard browser element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.36599999999999,
          "end": 156.36599999999999,
          "en": "and it does have a showModal method on its dom object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157,
          "end": 158.86599999999999,
          "en": "which I'm calling here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.86599999999999,
          "end": 161.7,
          "en": "And this will then simply open this dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.7,
          "end": 165.5,
          "en": "So I'm using some built-in browser features here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.633,
          "end": 169.166,
          "en": "And then there also is an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.166,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "or service in this shared folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.633,
          "en": "And in there I have some Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.633,
          "end": 176.566,
          "en": "which I expose as a read-only Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.566,
          "end": 180.166,
          "en": "And I have a method for setting it to an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.166,
          "end": 181.466,
          "en": "and for clearing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.466,
          "end": 183.533,
          "en": "so to setting it back to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.5,
          "end": 185.966,
          "en": "And the idea now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.966,
          "end": 189.533,
          "en": "that we could try using this errorService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.533,
          "end": 191.566,
          "en": "for telling the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.566,
          "end": 194.066,
          "en": "that this error-modal should be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.433,
          "end": 197.03300000000002,
          "en": "And how could we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.03300000000002,
          "end": 199.933,
          "en": "Well, for a start, we should go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.933,
          "end": 204.733,
          "en": "where the error might occur, so in the places service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.766,
          "end": 208.333,
          "en": "here in addPlaceToUser and catchError.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.6,
          "end": 210.433,
          "en": "Here I want to use this errorService to inform it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.466,
          "end": 218.333,
          "en": "that an error occurred so that then in the second step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.333,
          "end": 222.9,
          "en": "any interested parties can react to that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.9,
          "end": 225.5,
          "en": "and for example, show that error-modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.933,
          "end": 229.133,
          "en": "So therefore, here in the places service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.133,
          "end": 233.5,
          "en": "we can and should inject the errorService like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.3,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "Make sure to also import the errorService of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.133,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "And with it injected, we can use it here in catchError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.566,
          "end": 252.3,
          "en": "and call showError.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.033,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "And here I'll then simply output that same error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.233,
          "end": 267.233,
          "en": "Now we just need to listen to this Signal here somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.33299999999997,
          "end": 270.666,
          "en": "We need to react to changes in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.866,
          "end": 274.966,
          "en": "And a good place could be the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.966,
          "end": 277.133,
          "en": "the RootComponent of our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.6,
          "end": 282.133,
          "en": "There, we can also inject the errorService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 283.733,
          "end": 286.733,
          "en": "by calling inject, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.933,
          "end": 293.8,
          "en": "of course you must make sure as always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 293.8,
          "end": 296.33299999999997,
          "en": "that all the things are imported into this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 297.433,
          "end": 299.33299999999997,
          "en": "And then we can add a Signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 300.233,
          "end": 303.533,
          "en": "which simply exposes the error Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 303.533,
          "end": 305.566,
          "en": "provided by the errorService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 308.633,
          "end": 311.266,
          "en": "And now in the app component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.366,
          "end": 314.2,
          "en": "at the very top of it, maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 314.2,
          "end": 316.666,
          "en": "we can render the modal, the error-modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 316.666,
          "end": 318.33299999999997,
          "en": "which is part of the shared folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 318.33299999999997,
          "end": 321.266,
          "en": "that was attached, conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 321.266,
          "end": 325.3,
          "en": "We can check if the error Signal has a truthy value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 325.3,
          "end": 328.666,
          "en": "and if it does, we can render app-error-modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.33299999999997,
          "end": 333.3,
          "en": "and make sure that this is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 333.3,
          "end": 336.733,
          "en": "to the imports error array of the app component, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 339.033,
          "end": 341.8,
          "en": "and that it's imported into the file as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 344.5,
          "end": 348.133,
          "en": "And then to app error-modal, pass a title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 348.133,
          "end": 349.9,
          "en": "which can be a hard-coded string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 349.9,
          "end": 353.1,
          "en": "and therefore doesn't need any property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 353.1,
          "end": 356.2,
          "en": "or something like this, like, \"An error occurred!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 358.033,
          "end": 360.766,
          "en": "And the message is then a bound property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.766,
          "end": 362.966,
          "en": "because I want to bind it to the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 362.966,
          "end": 365.2,
          "en": "that's stored in the error Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 367.066,
          "end": 370.133,
          "en": "And with that, this modal should be shown conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 370.133,
          "end": 373.733,
          "en": "if an error occurs with help of that errorService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 373.733,
          "end": 374.933,
          "en": "and that modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 376.166,
          "end": 378.033,
          "en": "So now if you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 378.033,
          "end": 382.9,
          "en": "and I still have that error in my backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 382.9,
          "end": 385.33299999999997,
          "en": "so I'm still returning that error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 385.33299999999997,
          "end": 386.766,
          "en": "no matter what happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 387.83299999999997,
          "end": 390.566,
          "en": "and therefore if I now click on one of these elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 390.566,
          "end": 392.266,
          "en": "you see that modal opens up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 393.433,
          "end": 396.1,
          "en": "and if I click okay, it goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 396.1,
          "end": 399.933,
          "en": "And that's one way how you could handle an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 399.933,
          "end": 402.8,
          "en": "that occurs due to some request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 402.8,
          "end": 405.3,
          "en": "that's sent from a different Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 405.3,
          "end": 408.166,
          "en": "than where you want to handle it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 408.166,
          "end": 409.966,
          "en": "As always, and as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 409.966,
          "end": 413.033,
          "en": "it's not the only way of handling this, but it's one way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 414.133,
          "end": 417.3,
          "en": "And with that I'll get rid of that error code in the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 418.366,
          "end": 420.333,
          "en": "and restart that server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 420.333,
          "end": 421.366,
          "en": "and move on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 421.366,
          "end": 425.033,
          "en": "so that we can finally finish this demo application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
